    {
      "id": "ym1dgwn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. List of Fundamental Rights"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Articles 12–13 define the State and establish judicial review to protect Fundamental Rights.",
        "Articles 14–18 outline the Right to Equality along with specific constitutional exceptions.",
        "Articles 19–22 ensure the Right to Freedom while allowing reasonable restrictions.",
        "Articles 23–24 establish the Right against Exploitation, prohibiting human trafficking and forced labor.",
        "Articles 32–35 grant the Right to Constitutional Remedies through various types of writs."
      ],
      "id": "djb8r4m"
    },
